rising from relatively undignified  beginnings  this mysterious bounty hunter has become  one of the most iconic characters in the  star wars galaxy but that hasn't made  him immune from a series of  misconceptions here's a look at some  things you may  incorrectly believe about boba fett  although boba fett wears the same type  of armor as the titular protagonist of  the mandalorian  he isn't part of the mandalorian creed  at least not always  donald f glutt's empire strikes back  novelization states that boba was part  of  a group of evil warriors defeated by the  jedi knights during the clone wars  moreover daniel keys morin's novella the  last one standing a tale of boba fett  which was published in kevin j  anderson's 1996 anthology novel  tales of the bounty hunters gave boba a  real name jaster mirel  and claimed that he was exiled from his  home world of mandalore  this story was canon until george lucas  changed boba's origin  for episode 2 attack of the clones to  make him the unaltered clone and son  of bounty hunter jango fett lucas has  never explained the reasoning behind  this change but morin was ultimately not  upset about it  in a 2018 interview the author noted  that lucas had already changed plenty of  his own previous ideas about star wars  so he wasn't surprised when the  legendary creator decided to alter those  of another writer  chewbacca spent years in boba fett's  crosshairs due to his longtime  friendship with han solo but that  doesn't mean that fett hates all wookies  in fact the darth vader comics reveal  boba worked alongside a wookie named  black persanten when the two were both  employed by job of the hutt and boba  even vouched for the wookie when vader  brought up the possibility of failure  before vader assigned chrysanthen to  capture an agent of the emperor  he ended up going toe-to-toe with  obi-wan kenobi in the comic star wars  number 20 because  jabba tasked cursantin with capturing  the man who kept interfering with the  collection of his water attacks  later in the series kursantin would go  on to fight chewbacca and darth vader  number 14  while trying to capture han solo so  while boba definitely has beef with at  least one wookie  he's capable of getting along with  others opening a previously unknown  chapter in their shared past  marvel comics revealed that boba fett  and luke skywalker met long before they  crossed paths and the empire strikes  back after the events of a new hope  darth vader traveled to tatooine and  assigned boba to hunt down a rebel pilot  associated with a man named obi-wan  kenobi and a smuggling vessel called the  millennium falcon  vader also specified to bring this pilot  back in one piece  boba tracked this bounty down to ben  kenobi's home in the jungle and wastes  and temporarily blinded him with a flash  grenade but the mysterious rebel held  his own against boba  and narrowly escaped his clutches after  all that boba must have been happy to  take a shot at luke and empire even  though boba failed to capture his rebel  quarry  he did give vader a name skywalker for  boba that name wasn't familiar  but for vader it made him rethink  everything emperor palpatine had told  him about the fates of his children  this information may explain why vader  appeared to remain  so calm when the emperor first mentioned  the name skywalker  in empire strikes back boba fett was a  killer even before mace windu  decapitated his father  in attack of the clones in fact when  bova was growing up  django taunt his boy the same skills he  learned as a bounty hunter  including survival and martial arts in  the 2019 comic age of republic  jango fett number one django takes boba  on a mission with three other bounty  hunters as part of his training  the mission is to capture a twilight  girl and return her to her father  but after they find this bounty the  other hunters threaten to kill boba if  he doesn't hand over the twilight girl  of course these two bounty hunters  underestimate the boy  and boba kills them both without his  father's help the comic ends with boba  asking his father if he did all right to  which django responds  you shot well you trusted your judgment  and you've started building your  reputation  a father couldn't ask for a better start  for his son's legacy we don't get a ton  of insight into django's parenting but  at least he cared about his son enough  to prepare him for a galaxy that might  not welcome him with open arms  the current star wars canon portrays  young boba as someone in pursuit of his  father's killer  after the events of attack of the clones  one story arc from the popular animated  series  star wars the clone wars sees boba team  up with bounty hunters ara singh  bosk and costas and impersonate a clone  cadet in order to infiltrate a republic  vessel called the endurance  and kill mace windu in order to gain  vengeance for windu's murder of jango  fett  when the crew ends up taking hostages  however boba begins to become conflicted  about the job  even if it means avenging his father one  of the ark's strengths is that it shows  a post attack of the clones boba as  sympathetic and not just a ruthless  killing machine  this arc sets up the code of honor that  bobo would continue to establish and  refine as he grew into adulthood  boba fett's first movie appearance came  in the empire strikes back but it wasn't  his screen debut  what if he doesn't survive he's worth a  lot to me  boba's first appearance in the star wars  universe actually came during an  animated segment from the infamous 1978  star wars holiday  special which was aired in part to  further stoke anticipation for the  empire strikes back the short seas luke  c-3po and r2d2 crash land on the water  moon of pana  to save han solo and chewbacca who have  also crash-landed  luke 3po and r2 run into boba fett who  saves them from a giant monster with a  weapon similar to the sniper rifle we  now see in the mandalorian  and they decide to team up unfortunately  r2 later finds out that boba is darth  vader's right hand man  despite all its numerous flaws the  holiday special will always have the  honor of giving us boba fett's first  media appearance  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite star wars characters are  coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one
 

