nderestimate the boy  and boba kills them both without his  father's help the comic ends with boba  asking his father if he did all right to  which django responds  you shot well you trusted your judgment  and you've started building your  reputation  a father couldn't ask for a better start  for his son's legacy we don't get a ton  of insight into django's parenting but  at least he cared about his son enough  to prepare him for a galaxy that might  not welcome him with open arms  the current star wars canon portrays  young boba as someone in pursuit of his  father's killer  after the events of attack of the clones  one story arc from the popular animated  series  star wars the clone wars sees boba team  up with bounty hunters ara singh  bosk and costas and impersonate a clone  cadet in order to infiltrate a republic  vessel called the endurance  and kill mace windu in order to gain  vengeance for windu's murder of jango  fett  when the crew ends up taking hostages  however boba begins to become conflicted  about the job  even if it means avenging his father one  of the ark's strengths is that it shows  a post attack of the clones boba as  sympathetic and not just a ruthless  killing machine  this arc sets up the code of honor that  bobo would continue to establish and  refine as he grew into adulthood  boba fett's first movie appearance came  in the empire strikes back but it wasn't  his screen debut  what if he doesn't survive he's worth a  lot to me  boba's first appearance in the star wars  universe actually came during an  animated segment from the infamous 1978  star wars holiday  special which was aired in part to  further stoke anticipation for the  empire strikes back the short seas luke  c-3po and r2d2 crash land on the water  moon of pana  to save han solo and chewbacca who have  also crash-landed  luke 3po and r2 run into boba fett who  saves them from a giant monster with a  weapon similar to the sniper rifle we  now see in the mandalorian  and they decide to team up unfortunately  r2 later finds out that boba is darth  vader's right hand man  despite all its numerous flaws the  holiday special will always have the  honor of giving us boba fett's first  media appearance  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite star wars characters are  coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one


